What the hardware tools of FreeBSD 16.0-CURRENT, NetBSD 11.0, OpenBSD 8.0
and DragonFly 6.4.2 print on a virtual machine (bhyve, UEFI): a virtio
disk, network adapter and random number generator, a framebuffer without a
DRM driver, an xHCI controller with a USB tablet, the PS/2 keyboard and
mouse.  No Wi-Fi, no sound, no Bluetooth.  Captured on 2026-11-01 for
lib/hwprobe.py and tests/test_hwprobe.py.

<os>/<command>.out is what the command printed, .rc its exit status
(FreeBSD's `devmatch -p` and NetBSD's `drvctl -t` are usage errors, kept as
captured).  On OpenBSD the kernel of the installer refuses pcidump(8), and
usbdevs(8) lists only the root hub (the port of the tablet is disabled).

Changed from what the tools printed: MAC addresses and the serial of the
tablet are made up (the MAC addresses in the documentation range of RFC
7042), the build hosts in the kernel version lines are example.test names;
uname and the error outputs are not kept.

Edited after capture: dragonfly/dmesg.out line 24 (the local APIC count)
carries a trailing `# gitleaks:allow` note, because gitleaks reads
"lapic_count=2" as an API key; the line plays no part in detection.
